{"authored" [{"question" "q-161511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-3),\\,\\sqrt{2t},\\,{t}^{5}⟩$ at $t=2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "f945047955e33b6065b36bf5537f6934c9065f79a354f7c7f7118ad50c801644" "basis" 1268 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate, we substitute $t=2$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{2}-3),\\sqrt{2(2)},{2}^{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1),\\sqrt{4},{2}^{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,2,32⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $f(t)$ at $t=2$ is the vector $⟨0,2,32⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/state.json" "file_sha256" "f945047955e33b6065b36bf5537f6934c9065f79a354f7c7f7118ad50c801644" "basis" 1268 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64c68ca974ad10c77d63faf7ee266208d4c766b30c27e9d04d0fc12a5d19bb3a" "basis" 1268 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037455/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_wid