tute at $s=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$  into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,i+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,j-k \\\\  & =1\\,i+1\\,j-k \\\\  & =i+j-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of  $f(s)$ at $s=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$  is $i+j-k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-160769" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0a1fc444872b67790a7f3251887a3968d6f0a1464f8ed52aa0d40cd75d4f9397"} {"question" "q-160769" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-160769" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-i-j+k"] ["math" "-i-j-k"] ["math" "i+j+k"] ["math" "i+j-k"] ["math" "i-j+k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-160769" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "i+j-k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-160788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t+1} \\\\ 1-{t}^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\end{aligned}]$ at $t=0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-160788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate, we substitute $t=0$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(0)+1} \\\\ 1-(0)^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(0)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the value of $f(t)$ at $t=0$ is $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-160788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0a1fc444872b67790a7f3251887a3968d6f0a1464f8ed52aa0d40cd75d4f9397"} {"question" "q-160788" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-160788" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-160788" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-161511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the value of $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-3),\\,\\sqrt{2t},\\,{t}^{5}⟩$ at $t=2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-161511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate, we substitute $t=2$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({2}^{2}-3),\\sqrt{2(2)},{2}^{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1),\\sqrt{4},{2}^{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,2,32⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $f(t)$ at $t=2$ is the vector $⟨0,2,32⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-161511" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0a1fc444872b67790a7f3251887a3968d6f0a1464f8ed52aa0d40cd75d4f9397"} {"question" "q-161511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-161511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨0,2,32⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,\\sqrt{2},32⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,2,16⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,2,8⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,\\sqrt{2},32⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-161511" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,2,32⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-348674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨{2}^{t-1},\\,\\frac{4}{t+1}⟩,$ what is $|r(1)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|r(1)|=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-348674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Evaluating the function at $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =⟨{2}^{0},\\,\\frac{4}{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(1)| & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-348674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0a1fc444872b67790a7f3251887a3968d6f0a1464f8ed52aa0d40cd75d4f9397"} {"question" "q-348674" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-348674" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-348691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{t+3},\\,3\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩,$ what is $|r(1)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|r(1)|=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-348691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Evaluating the function at $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =⟨\\sqrt{1+3},\\,3\\,{e}^{1-1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{4},\\,3\\,{e}^{0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(1)| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-348691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0a1fc444872b67790a7f3251887a3968d6f0a1464f8ed52aa0d40cd75d4f9397"} {"question" "q-348691" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"} {"question" "q-348691" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{13}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040107/state.json" "file_sha256" "be4dd0990636a27c88aa0ebaeb2c3e14a0a7476759a3d40b63516734dd14f9ba"}] "usage" {"q-161511" []} "basis" 1412 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186296771 17592186296772 17592186296773 17592186296774 17592186296775] "immutable_fields" [[17592186296770 :answer-field/correct] [17592186296770 :answer-field/id] [17592186296770 :answer-field/key] [17592186296770 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
